par2go patch to par2cmdline-turbo v1.5.0-20261005 (GPL-2.0-or-later, as upstream).

Scanning a file for a set's blocks, a block that matches only entries
already found gives no entry, and the scan moves one byte on (ScanDataFile:
"if (duplicate && false) // ignore duplicates"). Inside a run of one byte
longer than a block -- the megabytes of zeros a Matroska muxer reserves at
a file's start -- the block one byte on is the same bytes: its checksum
matches the same entries, the whole block is hashed again to learn that
they are the same, and so at every offset of the run. A 7 GB file with a
2.66 MiB run of zeros, scanned against a set of 1 MiB blocks that holds a
block of zeros, cost 1.7 million MD5s of 1 MiB: half an hour on one core,
with no read. par2cmdline 2.0.0 does the same.

Keep the length of the run of one byte the window ends with as the window
moves (one compare a step, a look back along the block after a jump), and
when a lookup of a block that is one byte repeated gives no entry, take
the block one byte on for the same for as long as that byte keeps coming,
without looking it up. An entry that has been found stays found, so the
answer is the one the lookup would give. A short block at the end of a
file, a lookup made expecting an entry, and a skip ahead (-S) all end the
run.

diff --git a/include/par2/filechecksummer.h b/include/par2/filechecksummer.h
index e68717e..fa99518 100644
--- a/include/par2/filechecksummer.h
+++ b/include/par2/filechecksummer.h
@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@ public:
   bool ShortBlock(void) const;
   u64 BlockLength(void) const;
 
+  // The last byte of the block in the window, and how many bytes at the
+  // block's end are that byte: the block's length when it is one byte
+  // repeated. (par2go patch; offered upstream.)
+  char WindowLastByte(void) const;
+  u64 WindowTailRun(void) const;
+
   // Return the current file offset
   u64 Offset(void) const;
 
@@ -126,6 +132,29 @@ private:
   FileCheckSummer& operator=(const FileCheckSummer &);
 };
 
+// The last byte of the block in the window
+
+inline char FileCheckSummer::WindowLastByte(void) const
+{
+  return outpointer[blocksize - 1];
+}
+
+// How many bytes at the end of the block in the window are its last byte
+
+inline u64 FileCheckSummer::WindowTailRun(void) const
+{
+  // One byte repeated: each byte is the one before it
+  if (blocksize < 2 || 0 == memcmp(outpointer, outpointer + 1, (size_t)blocksize - 1))
+    return blocksize;
+
+  const char *last = &outpointer[blocksize - 1];
+  const char *p = last;
+  while (p > outpointer && p[-1] == *last)
+    --p;
+
+  return (u64)(last - p) + 1;
+}
+
 // Return the current checksum
 
 inline u32 FileCheckSummer::Checksum(void) const
